// Generated by build.rs from `tables/region_060988.hex` +
// `tables/region_060988_index.csv` (round 33) — the 24-slice ESC
// extension table cluster (file 0x60988..0x61200, VMA 0x1c261588..
// 0x1c261e00, 2168 bytes). Per `docs/video/msmpeg4/spec/08-descriptor-
// constants.md` §1 / §2 each G-descriptor's `+0x0c..+0x18` pointer
// block addresses four of the slices: sub-A level-extension, sub-B
// level-extension (`+0x0c / +0x10`, byte arrays read at stride 4),
// and sub-A run-extension, sub-B run-extension (`+0x14 / +0x18`, u32
// arrays at stride 4). The kernel reads these only on first-tier and
// second-tier ESC paths; the general-path dequant uses
// `[esi+0x13c] / [esi+0x140]` (PQUANT-derived) per `spec/07` §4.1 and
// `spec/08` §1.3.
//
// Defines:
//   - ESC_EXT_SLICE_COUNT: usize (= 24)
//   - ESC_EXT_CLUSTER_BYTES: usize (= 2168)
//   - ESC_EXT_SLICE_<i>: &[u8] for i in 0..24 (slice in CSV order)
//   - ESC_EXT_SLICES: [&[u8]; 24]
//   - ESC_EXT_SLICE_META: [(usize relative_offset, u32 vma, usize length); 24]
//   - ESC_EXT_G{0,1,2,3,4,5}_SLICE_INDICES: [usize; 4]
//     (the four cluster-slice indices that match each G-descriptor's
//     `(+0x0c, +0x10, +0x14, +0x18)` pointer block per `spec/08` §2.2 /
//     `spec/14` §2.1)
//
// **Slice-content semantics remain spec-OPEN per `spec/08` §4.1.** The
// kernel reads `[base + idx*4]` (BYTE for `+0x0c/+0x10`, DWORD for
// `+0x14/+0x18`) but the slices' record format is mechanically
// `(symbol_u32_le, bit_length_u32_le)` 8-byte pairs; the relationship
// between the two — and whether the slices are themselves secondary
// canonical-Huffman sources — is not yet pinned down. Round 33 wires
// the bytes and per-descriptor attribution only.
include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/esc_ext_cluster.rs"));

